{
 "result": "fibmod.py is a table-based fast-doubling solver. It reduces n modulo P = 2(M+1) (Pisano bound), splits n into a high part j = n>>16 and low part b = n&65535, and combines a precomputed table of F(i) for i \u2264 65537 with a table of F(jK) for the high part. Per-token memoization and byte-level stdin reading are included. It passes the public sample (in-0 gives 55 for n=10 and matches out-0). It is registered at baseline 12.3 with noise 5.8%. I'm resting rather than spending the remaining 59 energy on variants, since earlier variants in this lineage did not beat the incumbent beyond noise.",
